 and infrared LEDs designed to  minimize wrinkles and heal inflamed  blemishes there is actually quite a good  evidence based around LED and  near-infrared which is what this device  has because actually those sorts of  wavelengths of light can penetrate down  to the dermis and can actually stimulate  a little bit of collagen function so I  think this device is not too bad does it  feel quite hot in there Katie  little bit I feel like I'm like  sunbathing  right device number two this is the zip  it's a nano current skincare device so I  want you to go ahead and take your face  and your neck get in with the gel then  so talk to me about what a nano current  skincare device actually is so according  to the manufacturers this uses light  electrical stimulation to penetrate the  skin and then they say that it boosts  the production of something called ATP  which is an enzyme which is in all cells  your skin cells then regenerate like  boots and metabolism and you get skin  rejuvenation now the makers of the Zips  say that users could see results in just  four weeks does that sound right to you  well I'm a bit dubious about that so  every time I do any form of anti-aging  treatment with my patients I'll say that  it does take a bit longer than that  because of the way that the skin cells  cycle to actually see a biological  effect it often does take 8 to 12 weeks  the mindful touch is an invitation to  reconnect to your senses now our third  item is happening inside this tent what  is apparently 99.9% pure and I can I'll  show you the tech bit now look at this  skin bubble  another helpful volunteer Nicola is  having a facial that begins with an  eight-minute virtual reality video to  help put her in a state of mindfulness  which in turn releases oxytocin a happy  neuro chemical which then apparently  helps the skin better absorb the product  so I love mindfulness and I think it can  be really really helpful for skin  conditions which can be affected by  stress so thing